.TH SRS-GUI 1 "October 2026" "srs-sysinfo 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
srs-gui \- SRS system information viewer (GTK 3)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B srs-gui
[\fB\-\-gui\-open=\fIPANEL\fR[,\fIPANEL\fR...]] [\fB\-\-gui\-tray\fR] [\fB\-\-gui\-classic\fR | \fB\-\-gui\-new\fR]
.br
.B srs-gui
\fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B srs-gui
is the graphical front end of SRS, a Linux system information viewer inspired by
SIV64X (System Information Viewer by Ray Hinchliffe, RH Software) and built to improve on it.
SRS is an independent project, not affiliated with SIV or its author. It shows CPU,
memory, sensor, storage, bus, GPU, network and operating-system information,
and includes a CPU burn-in / stress tester and benchmarks.
SRS is not affiliated with or endorsed by RH Software.
.PP
The main window (new in 2.0) has a sidebar of pages: Overview, Processor, Memory,
Motherboard & BIOS, Graphics & audio, Storage, Network, Sensors, USB & PCI devices,
Operating system, Benchmarks & stress and Tools. The Overview answers "Is my PC OK?" with a
status light per check (temperatures against each sensor's own limit, drive health, hardware
errors, free disk space, memory in use, sensor alarms) and cards with the key facts. Each other
page shows key facts and the items as tabs; "All N items" lists every item of the page. The
search box (\fBCtrl+F\fR) finds any item by name or id.
.PP
The classic view is the SIV-style interface of SRS 1.1: a main window with SIV's button row and
every item in its own panel. Open it with Menu \(-> Classic View, or start in it with
\fB\-\-gui\-classic\fR or the option "Start in classic view".
.PP
Root-only data (SMBIOS serials, DIMM SPD, SMART, ACPI tables, MSRs) is read
from a cache filled by
.BR srs-root (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-gui\-open= PANEL
Open the named items or tools at start: in the main window an item opens on its page, in the
classic view as its own panel. For example
.BR sensors ", " processors ", " burnin ", " stress ", " bench ", " ipi ", " latency ", " pi ", " crypto ", " prime ", " cachemem ", " storagebench ", " idlookup ", " find .
.TP
.B \-\-gui\-tray
start in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-gui\-classic
start in the classic view: the SIV-style main window with its button row, every item in its own panel.
.TP
.B \-\-gui\-new
start in the main window with the sidebar (Overview and one page per category), even when
"Start in classic view" is set in the options.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Print the command-line help or the version and exit (these are shared with
.BR sysreport-search (1)).
.SH USER GUIDE
Every tab and panel has a \fBGuide\fR button (also \fBF1\fR, and "Open guide for this item"
in its right-click menu) that opens the user guide at that item's section: in
Okular, Evince or Papers at the right page, otherwise the HTML guide in the web
browser. \fBMenu \(-> User Guide\fR opens the start; \fBShift+F1\fR opens the Help panel.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SRS_OPEN
panels to open at start, as for \fB\-\-gui\-open\fR.
.TP
.B SRS_DOC_DIR
directory holding the user guide (default /usr/share/doc/srs-sysinfo).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/srs-sysinfo/SRS-User-Guide.pdf, /usr/share/doc/srs-sysinfo/html/SRS-User-Guide.html
the user guide (PDF and HTML), with its Markdown sources in the same folder.
.TP
.I ~/.config/srs/SRSDEF.ini
settings (theme, update interval, tray, "Classic View=1" for Start in classic view, ...).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/srs/root/
root-only data collected by srs-root.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/srs/burnin\-YYYYMMDD\-HHMMSS.txt
the summary of each finished CPU Burnin / CPU Stress run.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/srs/bench\-history.tsv
one line per SRS Pi, Crypto and Prime Sieve run (time, test, settings, result, build).
.TP
.I /usr/share/hwdata/pci.ids, /usr/share/hwdata/usb.ids
device name databases.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysreport-search (1),
.BR srs-root (1),
.BR srs-sysreport (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/eugenesflanagin-spec/srs-sysinfo
